+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos – Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Optional due date per todo, server-computed `overdue`, overdue filter in API and list page (ticket #1).
+
+**Architecture:** `TodoStore` stores `DueDate` and computes overdue from an injected `TimeProvider` (UTC date). The API maps `Todo` to a `TodoResponse` that adds `overdue`; `PATCH` distinguishes absent vs. `null` via an `Optional<T>` struct with a JSON converter. `Home.razor` shows date and marker and filters through the store.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, minimal API, Blazor interactive server, xUnit, `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-faelligkeitsdatum-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages (no `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing`; write own fake clock).
+- Validation errors are `ValidationException` from `TodoStore`; malformed input → 400 `{"error": "..."}` via existing middleware.
+- TDD: failing test first. Every new UI element has a `data-testid`: `overdue-filter`, `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`.
+- Overdue ⇔ `DueDate is not null && DueDate < today && !Done`; today = `DateOnly.FromDateTime(time.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime)`.
+- API date format `"yyyy-MM-dd"`; page format `dd.MM.yyyy` (invariant culture). Copy: `fällig <date>`, `überfällig`, `nur überfällige`.
+- No sorting, no styling/colors, no date input in the UI, filter not persisted.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. A past-due todo marked done via `PATCH {"done":true}` must stop being overdue and drop out of `?overdue=true` → Task 2 test `DoneTodoLeavesOverdueFilter`.
+2. `PATCH {"title":"X"}` on a todo with a date must keep the date → Task 2 test `PatchWithoutDueDateKeepsIt`.
+3. Wrong date formats (`"20.11.2026"`, `"2026-13-40"`) must give 400, not 500 → Task 2 test `RejectsInvalidDueDates`.
+4. `GET /todos?overdue=yes` must give 400, not 500 → Task 2 test `RejectsInvalidOverdueQuery`.
+5. Today's due date at 23:30 UTC is still not overdue (UTC, not local) → Task 1 test `DueTodayIsNotOverdue` uses a clock at `2026-11-13T23:30:00Z`.
+
